# NestJS DTO Generation Pattern

Use this as the canonical pattern when creating or updating DTO files inside `src/modules/**/dto`. Do not inspect any files except entity in the same module.

## Source of Truth

- Read fields only from `src/modules/<module>/entities/*.entity.ts` in the same module.
- DTO field candidates are scalar entity columns (`@Column`, `@PrimaryColumn`).
- Ignore relation properties (`@ManyToOne`, `@OneToMany`, `@OneToOne`, `@ManyToMany`).
- Do not copy inherited base-model fields unless explicitly present as module DTO requirements.

## Required Files and Classes

- `create.dto.ts` -> `Create<Module>Dto`
- `update.dto.ts` -> `Update<Module>Dto extends PartialType(Create<Module>Dto)` + required id field
- `params.dto.ts` -> `<Module>UniqueParams` with required id field for route params

## Required Imports Pattern

```typescript
import { ValidationErrors } from 'nestjs-typeorm-shared'
import { ApiProperty, PartialType } from '@nestjs/swagger'
import { Transform } from 'class-transformer'
import { IsBoolean, IsInt, IsNotEmpty, IsOptional, IsString } from 'class-validator'
import { i18nValidationMessage } from 'nestjs-i18n'
```

Use only needed decorators per file.

## Validation Mapping Rules

- `string` column -> `@IsString({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.STRING_FORMAT) })`
- `number` column -> `@IsInt({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NUMBER_FORMAT) })`
- `boolean` column -> `@IsBoolean({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.BOOLEAN_FORMAT) })`
- Required field -> add `@IsNotEmpty({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NOT_EMPTY) })`
- Optional/nullable field -> add `@IsOptional()` and `@ApiProperty({ required: false })`
- Required field -> `@ApiProperty()`
- Array fields -> `@ApiProperty({isArray: true, type: () => Type})`

## Update DTO Rules

- Must extend `PartialType(Create<Module>Dto)`.
- Must add required id field from entity primary key with `@IsInt`, `@IsNotEmpty`, and `@ApiProperty`.
- Do not redeclare non-id create fields unless there is a strong module-specific reason.

## Params DTO Rules

- Include only route id parameter field (usually entity primary key).
- Use same validation as in update dto id field

## Canonical Example (order-category)

Entity source (same module): `entities/order-category.entity.ts`

- Primary key: `category_id: number`
- Scalar columns: `category_name: string`, `parent_category_id?: number`, `order_type_prefix: string`, `is_report_excluded: boolean`

`create.dto.ts` example:

```typescript
export class CreateOrderCategoryDto {
  @IsString({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.STRING_FORMAT) })
  @IsNotEmpty({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NOT_EMPTY) })
  @ApiProperty()
  category_name: string

  @IsInt({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NUMBER_FORMAT) })
  @IsOptional()
  @ApiProperty({ required: false })
  parent_category_id?: number

  @IsString({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.STRING_FORMAT) })
  @IsNotEmpty({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NOT_EMPTY) })
  @ApiProperty()
  order_type_prefix: string

  @IsBoolean({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.BOOLEAN_FORMAT) })
  @IsOptional()
  @ApiProperty({ required: false })
  is_report_excluded?: boolean
}
```

`update.dto.ts` example:

```typescript
export class UpdateOrderCategoryDto extends PartialType(CreateOrderCategoryDto) {
  @IsInt({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NUMBER_FORMAT) })
  @IsNotEmpty({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NOT_EMPTY) })
  @ApiProperty()
  category_id: number
}
```

`params.dto.ts` example:

```typescript
export class OrderCategoryUniqueParams {
  @IsInt({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NUMBER_FORMAT) })
  @Transform((v) => Number(v.value))
  @IsNotEmpty({ message: i18nValidationMessage(ValidationErrors.NOT_EMPTY) })
  @ApiProperty()
  category_id: number
}
```
